^"stream"{
 >>[2026-10-27 17:22] implement — the app holds a line from ?spw= and lays it out as its anatomy: the word framed by its mode, parts on a ring in { }, ( ) and < > in their own regions, nesting as regions within regions, and recurring words in resonance. The line is the title and waits in the corner box. Verified in Chrome with home[hook]{software.art.practice}(atlas)<person>, and without ?spw the page keeps <concept> and hides the box. Nine app commits, local and unpushed.
 >>[2026-10-27 17:24] implement — the snapshot in workers/factshift-center/assets now holds the app's 6b67304 build without source maps, and version.json records the revision and the spw query key. check:workers passes. The snapshot is uncommitted here until the creator asks, and deploying it is the creator's step.
 >>[2026-10-27 17:55] implement — the phone pass, from the creator's live notes, committed in the app as e9a390d (local, unpushed) and carried into the snapshot. It covers: the focal mark's home above [...], with a tap that opens Spw and the menu or closes it and hands over the tool; noun labels with state marks; panels docked on phones, one surface at a time; a compact mode list; a node panel that stacks; quieter Spw panel text; the line reading; and the semantics fixes. tsc and vite build pass. Stills at 390 and 1440 show no page widening. The PLAN.md interaction contract records the rules.
 >>[2026-10-27 18:04] implement — a gesture grammar, as a demo in the app and uncommitted. One recognizer covers tap, hold, swipe and hold-then-drag, with a landing preview, a way back and a compass taught once. The focal mark takes the full grammar; a node takes hold to name and select. The menu's gestures row counts what was found. Driven with touch at 390px: every gesture landed. A stale click flag that would have swallowed the next tap after a swipe was found and bounded to the click that follows a release. Removing the old drag handlers also removed consent.scss, which nothing else used.
 >>[2026-10-27 18:24] implement — the creator's live notes, in the app's working tree. Handle: the mark is the open tool's bottom-left corner; Spw rests centered as a stage, the others rest at home, and a menu sends the handle home. Swipes are spatial: ↑ to the mode column (slide to choose), ↓ to the menu, → into the tool, ← back to the last mode. A swipe toward nothing shows the card. No words beside the mark. Spw panel: one quiet line, run and clear, primes removed, a form heading. The mode column is vertical again, and the menu keeps labels left and outlined buttons right with a light-filled on. Driven with touch at 390 and 1440: every arc landed, and the page held its width.
 >>[2026-10-27 18:38] implement — the creator found swipes colliding. A swipe's direction is now locked once it crosses its line. The mode column moved to ←: a quick ← puts the tool away; held or slid, it opens the column, and the same touch chooses a mode, by stepping or by landing on a square. → is the tool's default activation; ↑ shows the card; the handle is at z-index 1000. No tool is in hand at the start, and the menu's focus is a keyboard-only ring. Every path was driven with touch at 390.
 >>[2026-10-27 18:48] implement — the creator's next notes. Tap toggles the tool. Hold grips it; the possibilities card is gone from the hold, because it was a weak use. ← opens the mode column at once; the quick ← that put the tool away was undone. ↓ is the primary menu; → is the tool's default activation; ↑ adds a node named in place. The larger square is the tool's slot, taking the handle's gestures while it is empty. Holding or dragging the handle rings it and lifts its tool, and a dragged node is ringed. A sketch node is renamed by id, because quickAddNode's reinit rebuilds the collection. Every path was driven with touch at 390.
 >>[2026-10-27 18:51] implement — committed in the app as e601855 at the creator's ask, and carried into the snapshot without source maps; version.json records the revision, and check:workers passes.
 >>[2026-10-27 19:36] implement — the creator's next notes, in the app's working tree. The tool is now a handle (a drag carries at once, a tap shows or hides the lens) and a lens (the larger square, which takes the tap and the swipes). A node's verbs open in a ring on hold, or on a tap with no tool in hand. The [...] menu keeps factshift.com's alignment and five rows; its rows name end states, and a row is listed only while it has something to act on. The reflex panel fits a phone. Every path was driven with touch at 390.
 >>[2026-10-27 19:40] implement — the lens corner is the handle's center on every screen. The lens, the tool frame and the phone panels were placed up from a 100vh box, which on a phone with its address bar showing is not the visible height. They are now placed from the top, as the handle is. Committed in the app as 619432e at the creator's ask and carried into the snapshot.
 >>[2026-10-27 19:53] implement — the creator asked for touch and drag thought through. Three faults were found and fixed. The lens covered Spw's run button, so a tap meant for run closed the window. The handle teleported to a centered stage and back. And the handle and the lens could both toggle things. Now the lens is the closed tool's face and hides while a window is open; the handle's tap steps back (menu, then window, then lens); the handle stays put. Desktop gets edge grab bands, and clear moved inside the prompt. Driven with touch at 390 and with a mouse at 1440. Uncommitted.
 >>[2026-10-27 20:30] implement — the creator found nodes hard to select and to link. A tap with no tool in hand now selects or deselects, and a tap on empty canvas clears the selection. A node dropped on another links to it (the selection with it), and dropped again it unlinks; the target is ringed, dashed, while hovered. The hold keeps the verb ring. Driven with touch at 390. Uncommitted. Next, from the creator's questions: double-tap to rename, membership by drop with write-back to the held line, ordinal and common containers, and a canvas ring that spawns a container with a placeholder.
 >>[2026-10-27 21:45] implement — the creator's next run of notes, in the app's working tree. A double-tap renames a node in place. Drops into a container, reorders along an ordered body, and braces spawned from the canvas ring rewrite the held line (held-line.ts, editLine in line-anatomy.ts). Pinch resizes a node or zooms the stage. The menu became families of verbs, turned by a swipe or a ›. The lens tap opens the tool or primes it; → submits; the window sits on top of the lens. Found on the way: a node's picture layer took taps meant for its neighbor, and a ring opened under a finger took that finger's own click. Both are fixed. Every path was driven with touch at 390. Uncommitted.
 >>[2026-10-27 21:47] implement — committed in the app as f5e9ffc at the creator's ask and carried into the snapshot.
}

